 r←ReadmeIsDue packagePath;ns;attempts;firstAttempt;schedule;wanted
⍝ Tells whether the README of the package in `packagePath` should be fetched now.
⍝ A README is tried up to three times: straight away, 24 hours later, and one week after the
⍝ first try. More than one go is worth having because a first failure is often temporary -
⍝ GitHub unreachable, or a release tag pushed some time after the package was published -
⍝ while a third failure a week later is not going to be cured by a fourth.
⍝ 'ok' is final at once: a README is tied to a tag, and tags do not move.
 schedule←24 168                                    ⍝ Hours after the FIRST attempt, one per retry
 r←1
 :If ⍬≢ns←GetReadmeRecord packagePath
     :If 'ok'≡{0=ns.⎕NC ⍵:'' ⋄ ns⍎⍵}'status'
         r←0
     :Else
         attempts←{0=ns.⎕NC ⍵:0 ⋄ ns⍎⍵}'attempts'
         firstAttempt←{0=ns.⎕NC ⍵:0 ⋄ ns⍎⍵}'firstAttempt'
         ⍝ `attempts` counts the tries already made, so it indexes the wait before the next one.
         ⍝ Out of range means there is no next one: either all three are done, or this record predates
         ⍝ retries altogether, in which case its answer stands rather than being reopened.
         :If (attempts<1)∨(attempts>≢schedule)∨0=firstAttempt
             r←0
         :Else
             wanted←firstAttempt+3600×attempts⊃schedule
             r←wanted≤⊃20 ⎕DT⊂⎕TS                   ⍝ Code 20 is seconds, so hours are addable
         :EndIf
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
